[{:seon.task/name "definitions-from-the-compiler"
  :seon.task/plan "Lane LOOP (in flight). Each top-level form's definitions come from Jolt's analyzer (jolt.analyzer/*unit-tap*, Jolt 9e42a0d8): vars by kind, methods [multi dispatch], protocol impls [protocol type], the ns form and its requires, resolved refs (vars, macros, classes), arities, exact text; readback after the eval decides what actually ran. Applied per form through the run-ahead writer (225 us, flat; no waiting). Replaces seon.program/def-heads, def-form?, recording's form tests, names-in, ns-env, harvest's flagged guesses and the request-level :defs buffer (repl.clj:228). Design: notes/audit-2026-10-21/program-facts-draft.edn (inv4: 133/133 definitions agree with the runtime on 2,016 real agent forms). Main loads forms in the topological order of the real refs and ns requires."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.program-test/a-form-records-exactly-what-the-compiler-defined
                      seon.program-test/defmethod-extend-and-defrecord-merge-and-load-on-main
                      seon.program-cost-test/recording-a-form-is-flat-in-the-program}}
 {:seon.task/name "program-mutations-are-refused-at-merge"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner 2026-10-21: program code (what merges) does not call clojure.core/intern, alter-var-root, eval or load-string (loading code is an effect), and defines nothing inside a fn body (inline-def). The done rule refuses the branch naming the definition and the call, from the compiler's resolved refs (never text). The REPL still evaluates them; the merge judges. Platform and library code are not judged."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.program/definitions-from-the-compiler"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.program-test/a-program-calling-alter-var-root-is-refused-naming-it
                      seon.program-test/a-def-inside-a-fn-body-is-refused}}
 {:seon.task/name "tests-run-by-reach"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner 2026-10-21: \"I want faster iteration not a matrix with every run permutation\", and \"incremental tests even across worktrees based on test digest\" (AGENTS.md section 3, results are reused by input digest). Gap: `bin/test` (test/test_runner.clj, `test-runner/-main`) ran every deftest each time (266 tests, 5-8 min); `seon.program/reaching-tests` answered which tests reach a definition, but nothing keyed a result by what the test reaches or reused one. v1 (`~/src/seon` seon.test.cache) keyed a result by the test's reach digest and ran only tests with no result; its lesson kept here: inputs without program facts (resources, fixtures, the dependency pins, the launchers) are folded into every digest, never left out. Design, extending what exists: (1) `seon.program/reach-digests` gives each test of a db its reach digest: its own form, its namespace's ns form and non-defining forms, and every live form its `:form/refs` reach transitively (a var to the form that last defined it, a multimethod's methods, a protocol's extensions), each form digested once (`seon.error/digest`), plus the checkout's `:env` digest (every tracked file but src/test .clj, task files and prose: deps.edn, bin/, resources/ with the schemas contracts name, test fixtures, every submodule pin, Jolt's included), plus the whole tree's digest for a test reaching a tree reader (`seon.program/tree-readers`: slurp, file-seq). (2) `bin/test --reach [NS...]` imports src and test as program facts (`seon.source/import-tx`, the same facts root and agents record), computes the digests, reuses every green result stored at its digest and runs the rest, storing each result. (3) Results live in one content-addressed directory shared by every checkout and worktree (`:seon.config.source/test-results-dir`, ~/src/seon-jolt/test-results: one file per digest, written temp-then-rename through `seon.fx/write-file`), not the one store: a checkout's store is runs/store under that checkout, so a store cannot be shared across worktrees. A landing runs `bin/test --reach`: what the change reaches, minus what is green at its digest. A change selects exactly the tests reaching it, since a test's digest moves only when a form it reaches does (`seon.program/reaching-tests` is the inverse closure). Known gaps: a test reading a file by a reader outside `tree-readers` or resolving a var by name at run time is digested without it; importing the program costs about 10 s per run (incremental import by file is the next step)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.program-test/a-changed-function-changes-the-digests-of-exactly-the-tests-reaching-it
                      seon.program-test/a-second-run-with-nothing-changed-runs-nothing
                      seon.program-test/a-result-recorded-in-one-checkout-is-reused-in-another}}]
